detector_raw:
{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this production plan — to maximize total profit (unit price minus raw material cost minus processing cost), or to maximize total revenue, or to minimize total cost?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, presenting mutually exclusive options within one sentence."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are there any demand limits or minimum production requirements for each product, or can the factory produce any non-negative quantity of each product as long as equipment hours are not exceeded?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding production constraints (limits/minimums vs. non-negative quantities), which constitutes one independent semantic query."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the production quantities of the three products required to be whole numbers (integer pieces), or can they be treated as continuous (fractional) values?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the variable type (integer vs. continuous) for production quantities."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "In the table, the numbers under each product on each equipment (e.g., 5 for Product I on A1) — do these represent the processing time in hours required per piece of that product on that equipment?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for the definition of the numerical values in the table."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 2,
  "is_atomic": false,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the processing cost, is the cost per machine hour (e.g., 0.05 yuan/hour for A1) multiplied by the actual hours used on that equipment to get the total processing cost?",
    "Is this the only processing cost component (i.e., no fixed setup or batch costs)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains two semantically independent questions: one asking about the calculation method for variable processing costs, and another asking if there are additional fixed cost components."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For Product I, which can be processed on multiple equipment types at each stage (e.g., A1 or A2 for stage A, and B1, B2, or B3 for stage B), is it allowed to split the production of Product I across different equipment types at the same stage (e.g., some pieces on A1 and some on A2), or must all pieces of a given product use a single equipment type per stage?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether production can be split across equipment types or must be consolidated, which constitutes one independent policy choice."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For Product I, can the stage A and stage B equipment choices be made independently (e.g., some pieces processed on A1 for stage A and B3 for stage B, while other pieces use A2 for stage A and B1 for stage B), or must each piece follow a fixed pairing of A and B equipment?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the dependency between stage A and stage B equipment assignments."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any requirement that the number of pieces of a product completing stage A must equal the number completing stage B (i.e., no work-in-progress or inventory between stages), or can there be a mismatch between the two stages?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the relationship between completion counts at two stages, presenting a binary choice (must equal vs. can mismatch) which constitutes one independent query."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 2,
  "is_atomic": false,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the effective machine hours (e.g., 6000 for A1) the total available hours for the entire planning period?",
    "Is there only one planning period (i.e., no multi-period or time-indexed structure)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains two semantically independent questions: one asking about the scope of the machine hours (total vs. per period) and another asking about the temporal structure (single vs. multi-period). A user could confirm the hours are total without confirming the single-period structure, or vice versa."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are there any other constraints or costs I should be aware of, such as labor limits, quality requirements, or minimum utilization of any equipment?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single open-ended clarification question asking for any additional constraints or costs, with examples provided for context but not as separate sub-questions."
}
